# nouveau module set, in load order (documentation only; nothing reads this file at runtime). The .ko files come from
# the staged kernel build (k13: builder /build/dist, krel 6.18.21-android17-5-g3938c8d97142-dirty-ab16302624; k14:
# /build/dist14) via stage_kernel.py NATIVE_OPTIN: legacy layout /odm/lib/modules, payload layout (Phase 5)
# /odm/dgpu/lib/modules inside ESP:/gb/dgpu-<krel>.erofs.
# They are NEVER in modules.load / modules.load.late (NVIDIA_PLAN.md invariant 1): gb_nouveau.sh auto (gb_nouveau.rc)
# insmods them after sys.boot_completed, long after i915 has claimed card0/renderD128, only after its guards pass,
# and always with "runpm=1 modeset=2" last (plus whitelisted config=/debug= atoms, INTERFACES.md 7.4).
# Already loaded from modules.load (i915 deps): i2c-algo-bit.ko wmi.ko video.ko drm_display_helper.ko
drm_exec.ko
drm_gpuvm.ko
gpu-sched.ko
drm_ttm_helper.ko
nouveau.ko runpm=1 modeset=2
# mxm-wmi.ko: built (Kleaf must list it) but unused - nouveau calls mxm_wmi_supported() only with CONFIG_VGA_SWITCHEROO.
# Loading nouveau at boot from a load list is not supported: a nouveau oops freezes this machine (PANIC_ON_OOPS=y,
# panic=0) and would repeat on every boot; gb_nouveau.sh's crash-loop guard and kill switches only cover its own loads.
